WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.160
Were you aware of, once these students were enrolled, of their contact with your father [A.

2
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.380
P. Tureaud, Sr.] on what . . . how things were going for them?

3
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.300
A. P. TUREAUD, JR.: Oh yes, he constantly maintained contact with them [Roy Wilson, Daryle Foister, and Lutrill Payne].

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:22.580
He would also drive up to the campus if they were having problems of one kind or another and needed support.

5
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.140
He was more than . . . more than just their lawyer.

6
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.900
He was like a support system.

7
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:39.560
In some ways, without sounding mushy, he was really like a parent supporting their kid in an environment or young person in an environment.

8
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:48.300
Because a lot of those graduate students were well into their adulthood, they weren’t right out of high school.

9
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.420
He was very supportive.
